# Instance policies

Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.

Before you commit, send mail, deploy, or make a skill-invoke exception, load instance policy:

```bash
node .cursor/skills/autodevelop/scripts/policies-load.mjs
```

That script finds the repo-root workspace bind `.autodevelop/.policies/` first, then the legacy `.cursor/skills/<instance>/autodevelop/.policies/` the same way as `config.json` (first non-kit instance folder). It merges each live `*.yaml` over `POLICY_DEFAULTS` in `scripts/policy-defaults.mjs`. A missing folder uses those builtins. The CLI prints policy names and sources only — not allowlists, tokens, or message bodies.

Do not ship kit `*.example.yaml` policy files. Instance copies stay under `.autodevelop/.policies/` (legacy: `<instance>/autodevelop/.policies/`). Do not put a live instance folder in the plugin payload.

Branch names and ask flags: [branch-policy.mdc](branch-policy.mdc). Environment names, promote order, hosts, and hostnames: `environments-policy` (`/devops` reads that file). Hyperparameters: [configuration.mdc](configuration.mdc). Handbook table: [docs/configure.md](../../../../docs/configure.md).
